    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d131-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d131-f1-content">
                <p>Copies sent to London and Vienna.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d131-f2" n="2" xml:id="d131-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 4543 briefly summarized the French <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi>. (763.5/2–151)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d131-f3" n="3" xml:id="d131-f3-content">
                <p>The French text is not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d131-f4" n="4" xml:id="d131-f4-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d131-f5" n="5" xml:id="d131-f5-content">
                <p>Same as telegram 1850 to London, <ref target="frus1950v04#pg_494">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1950, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">iv</hi>, p. 494</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d131-f6" n="6" xml:id="d131-f6-content">
                <p>Telegram 4160 summarized the draft of the French <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi> and noted that it still needed clearance by the French
                    Ministry of Defense. (763.5/1–1851)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
